1
00:00:07,970 --> 00:00:11,097
[WIGGINS] Okay, everyone.
Keep back, it's dangerous here.

2
00:00:11,139 --> 00:00:13,183
Holmes had an
experiment backfire.

3
00:00:13,225 --> 00:00:15,853
And the explosion seems
to have blown up the flat.

4
00:00:15,895 --> 00:00:17,270
He says he'll offer all youse

5
00:00:17,312 --> 00:00:19,481
a free consultation
to make up for it.

6
00:00:19,523 --> 00:00:22,693
But right now,
he needs everyone to leave.

7
00:02:07,422 --> 00:02:09,299
[WATSON]
The Lord of Crime?

8
00:02:09,341 --> 00:02:12,302
So, Miss Adler was dealing
with him this entire time,

9
00:02:12,344 --> 00:02:14,054
and not the government
like she claimed.

10
00:02:14,096 --> 00:02:15,430
Are you absolutely
certain, Sherlock?

11
00:02:15,472 --> 00:02:18,058
[HOLMES groans]

12
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:20,644
Listen! We know
the man's a killer!

13
00:02:20,686 --> 00:02:23,522
I find it hard to believe
he'll keep any promise!

14
00:02:23,563 --> 00:02:26,316
It's not like we can just let
Adler walk out the door!

15
00:02:26,358 --> 00:02:28,110
No, it can't be that.

16
00:02:28,152 --> 00:02:30,863
It seems there's no way
to save her at this point.

17
00:02:30,904 --> 00:02:32,656
And, yet...

18
00:02:32,698 --> 00:02:33,532
Damn it all!

19
00:02:33,573 --> 00:02:34,574
[BOTH gasp]

20
00:02:34,616 --> 00:02:36,785
Concentrate!
There must be something else!

21
00:02:36,827 --> 00:02:39,079
So why can't I think of it?!

22
00:02:40,455 --> 00:02:43,042
What're you talking about?

23
00:02:43,083 --> 00:02:44,334
[HOLMES] It's hopeless.

24
00:02:44,376 --> 00:02:47,921
No matter what, I always
arrive at the same conclusion.

25
00:02:47,963 --> 00:02:50,215
All we can do is go with
the worst-case scenario.

26
00:02:50,256 --> 00:02:52,384
[footsteps]

27
00:02:55,261 --> 00:02:56,471
[HUDSON, WATSON grunt]

28
00:02:57,723 --> 00:02:59,307
[HUDSON]
Miss Adler.

29
00:02:59,349 --> 00:03:01,101
I haven't visited for very long,

30
00:03:01,143 --> 00:03:04,270
but thank you for
your hospitality.

31
00:03:04,312 --> 00:03:05,480
I was looking forward to having

32
00:03:05,522 --> 00:03:08,274
a long conversation
over some tea.

33
00:03:08,316 --> 00:03:11,778
[ADLER] Thank you,
Miss Hudson, as was I.

34
00:03:14,114 --> 00:03:15,824
[HOLMES] This really
is goodbye, isn't it?

35
00:03:15,866 --> 00:03:18,326
Oh, Sherly, don't tell
me you're going to miss me

36
00:03:18,368 --> 00:03:20,412
that much after
I'm out of your hair.

37
00:03:20,453 --> 00:03:22,372
I'm sure you'll recover.

38
00:03:22,414 --> 00:03:24,917
[chuckles] The "tough girl" act.

39
00:03:24,958 --> 00:03:27,335
[ADLER chuckles]

40
00:03:27,377 --> 00:03:28,837
[HOLMES]
Irene.

41
00:03:30,130 --> 00:03:31,715
This deal that's arranged--

42
00:03:31,757 --> 00:03:34,342
are you certain it's going to
save you in the end?

43
00:03:36,095 --> 00:03:37,554
Without a doubt.

44
00:03:37,596 --> 00:03:39,139
I may have messed
things up a bit,

45
00:03:39,181 --> 00:03:40,640
but I finally found a way out

46
00:03:40,682 --> 00:03:42,976
and can see the light
at the end of the tunnel.

47
00:03:43,018 --> 00:03:46,730
[HOLMES] She's bluffing,
and fully expects to be killed.

48
00:03:46,772 --> 00:03:49,566
Well, good. That's a relief.

49
00:03:49,608 --> 00:03:50,984
[HOLMES]
It was her fault for stealing

50
00:03:51,026 --> 00:03:53,779
something so pernicious.

51
00:03:53,820 --> 00:03:55,197
Still though,

52
00:03:55,239 --> 00:03:58,909
when it comes to her desire to
make the world a better place,

53
00:03:58,951 --> 00:04:01,954
there's nothing false behind it.

54
00:04:01,995 --> 00:04:06,374
It's up to me.
I have to keep her safe.

55
00:04:13,381 --> 00:04:14,925
[ALBERT] You really
believe this plan of yours

56
00:04:14,967 --> 00:04:17,302
will entice Sherlock
Holmes to show up?

57
00:04:17,343 --> 00:04:18,262
[WILLIAM]
Of course.

58
00:04:18,303 --> 00:04:20,513
I guarantee he'll
make an appearance.

59
00:04:20,555 --> 00:04:22,933
All for Irene Adler's sake.

60
00:04:22,975 --> 00:04:25,811
He has no interest in
the document itself.

61
00:04:25,852 --> 00:04:27,604
His first thought will likely be

62
00:04:27,646 --> 00:04:30,983
to safeguard Miss Adler from
any harm that would befall her.

63
00:04:31,024 --> 00:04:32,859
Which means he'll
be too distracted

64
00:04:32,901 --> 00:04:34,903
to uncover our identities.

65
00:04:34,945 --> 00:04:36,404
But the downside is

66
00:04:36,446 --> 00:04:38,698
unless Holmes receives
assurance Adler's life

67
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:40,993
is no longer in
any sort of danger,

68
00:04:41,034 --> 00:04:44,246
there's no chance of him
backing down, is there?

69
00:04:44,288 --> 00:04:47,791
Once again, we'll be
relying on you, Will.

70
00:04:47,833 --> 00:04:50,210
[WILLIAM]
Yes.

71
00:04:50,252 --> 00:04:53,088
I have a plan to
put his mind at ease.

72
00:05:11,940 --> 00:05:13,525
[OLD WOMAN]
Am I safe in presuming

73
00:05:13,566 --> 00:05:16,111
you're Miss Irene Adler?

74
00:05:16,153 --> 00:05:17,196
The gentleman you're to meet

75
00:05:17,237 --> 00:05:20,365
has already arrived
and is waiting for you.

76
00:05:20,406 --> 00:05:22,034
This way.

77
00:05:32,878 --> 00:05:36,215
[ALBERT]
Welcome, Irene Adler.

78
00:05:38,884 --> 00:05:40,844
[ADLER grunts]

79
00:05:40,886 --> 00:05:42,721
[ADLER]
I've brought the document,

80
00:05:42,762 --> 00:05:45,557
but please, allow me
to verify one thing.

81
00:05:46,474 --> 00:05:49,353
[ADLER] These reforms you
say will better the world.

82
00:05:49,394 --> 00:05:51,897
You swear you're
telling me the truth?

83
00:05:51,938 --> 00:05:55,525
[ALBERT] Of course,
our objectives are the same.

84
00:05:55,567 --> 00:05:58,111
However, if you
feel they don't align,

85
00:05:58,153 --> 00:06:01,698
you're free to
accuse me of such.

86
00:06:01,740 --> 00:06:03,616
I shall take your word.

87
00:06:03,658 --> 00:06:06,661
[ALBERT] All right then,
as a token of your loyalty,

88
00:06:06,703 --> 00:06:08,621
hand me the document.

89
00:06:17,214 --> 00:06:19,716
[HOLMES] Sorry, but you
can't turn it over yet.

90
00:06:19,758 --> 00:06:21,343
[gasps]

91
00:06:21,385 --> 00:06:23,762
Sherlock, wait!

92
00:06:23,803 --> 00:06:28,058
Well, Sherlock Holmes.
So, you did show up after all.

93
00:06:28,100 --> 00:06:31,103
You're the Lord of Crime?
We meet at last.

94
00:06:31,144 --> 00:06:34,064
[ADLER] Answer me.
What are you doing here?

95
00:06:34,106 --> 00:06:36,400
[HOLMES]
Keeping you safe, what else?

96
00:06:36,441 --> 00:06:37,734
[ADLER]
Seriously?

97
00:06:37,776 --> 00:06:41,029
[HOLMES] But don't worry.
I didn't come alone!

98
00:06:42,155 --> 00:06:47,619
- -[inhales]
- -[whistle sounds]

99
00:06:47,660 --> 00:06:49,662
Scotland Yard?!

100
00:06:49,704 --> 00:06:52,249
[HOLMES]
There's nowhere for you to run.

101
00:06:52,291 --> 00:06:54,542
It's over.

102
00:06:54,584 --> 00:06:56,502
You're going to get
yourself killed, too!

103
00:06:56,544 --> 00:07:01,258
Take it easy, Irene, and
let me handle this, all right?

104
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:03,802
But, Sherlock...

105
00:07:03,843 --> 00:07:07,764
[ALBERT chuckles] Are you
planning on arresting me?

106
00:07:07,806 --> 00:07:10,809
[HOLMES] That all
depends entirely on you.

107
00:07:10,850 --> 00:07:12,394
Go on then.

108
00:07:12,436 --> 00:07:14,729
[HOLMES] After learning the
contents of these papers,

109
00:07:14,771 --> 00:07:16,106
my first thought was naturally

110
00:07:16,148 --> 00:07:18,817
how I could protect
Irene from the fallout.

111
00:07:18,858 --> 00:07:21,320
As long as the possibility
exists she'll leak them,

112
00:07:21,361 --> 00:07:23,571
then regardless of what
happens to the documents,

113
00:07:23,613 --> 00:07:26,325
the government will still
try to eliminate her.

114
00:07:26,366 --> 00:07:28,076
Which presents one solution:

115
00:07:28,118 --> 00:07:30,412
Find some way to get
her out of the country.

116
00:07:30,454 --> 00:07:33,332
But the certitude of
that plan is in doubt.

117
00:07:33,373 --> 00:07:37,336
So, what can I do to
completely ensure her safety?

118
00:07:37,377 --> 00:07:40,630
The answer is to have her
protected by someone else.

119
00:07:40,672 --> 00:07:43,008
An individual operating in
the underworld of London

120
00:07:43,049 --> 00:07:45,593
who has complete autonomy.

121
00:07:45,635 --> 00:07:50,098
In other words, someone
like you, Lord of Crime.

122
00:07:50,140 --> 00:07:51,308
I hate to admit it,

123
00:07:51,350 --> 00:07:54,186
but you're the only one
capable of protecting her.

124
00:07:57,230 --> 00:07:59,983
Obviously, as I've
already informed her,

125
00:08:00,025 --> 00:08:02,486
part of our arrangement
is I keep her alive.

126
00:08:02,527 --> 00:08:05,155
No one else can offer
her the same guarantee.

127
00:08:05,197 --> 00:08:09,034
But I am sure it will take more
than my word to convince you.

128
00:08:11,577 --> 00:08:13,413
[BOTH grunt]

129
00:08:13,455 --> 00:08:16,833
[ALBERT] Irene Adler. Write
my name on this piece of paper,

130
00:08:16,875 --> 00:08:20,337
seal it in the envelope,
and hand it to him.

131
00:08:20,379 --> 00:08:22,922
Holmes, if there comes
a time when you determine

132
00:08:22,964 --> 00:08:26,551
she has been dispatched, you're
free to open the envelope,

133
00:08:26,592 --> 00:08:29,262
read my name,
and then come for me.

134
00:08:29,304 --> 00:08:31,890
Agree to place your trust
in me, Sherlock Holmes,

135
00:08:31,931 --> 00:08:36,978
and I will do the same for you.

136
00:08:37,020 --> 00:08:39,398
Fine by me.

137
00:08:39,439 --> 00:08:42,275
[pen scratching]

138
00:08:46,821 --> 00:08:48,365
[ADLER]
It's done.

139
00:08:51,201 --> 00:08:57,957
And I have it
in my possession.

140
00:08:57,999 --> 00:09:00,419
Then with that,
our business is concluded.

141
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:04,005
You may leave, along with your
so-called police force.

142
00:09:04,047 --> 00:09:04,839
[ADLER gasps]

143
00:09:04,881 --> 00:09:06,425
[HOLMES]
So, you knew all along?

144
00:09:06,466 --> 00:09:10,095
[ALBERT] Forgive me,
but I must take my leave.

145
00:09:10,136 --> 00:09:12,722
Farewell, Sherlock Holmes.

146
00:09:12,764 --> 00:09:15,559
[footsteps]

147
00:09:21,398 --> 00:09:24,526
[HOLMES] Generous of him to
allow us to say our goodbyes.

148
00:09:24,568 --> 00:09:26,611
[ADLER]
You've done so much for me.

149
00:09:26,652 --> 00:09:29,781
There's no possible way I could
ever express my gratitude.

150
00:09:29,822 --> 00:09:31,866
I'll pass your
thanks on to John.

151
00:09:31,908 --> 00:09:34,369
[ADLER] Until now, I've done
nothing but lie to you.

152
00:09:34,411 --> 00:09:37,330
So, I doubt you'll take my word
for this, but...

153
00:09:37,372 --> 00:09:41,084
...the truth is
I am rather fond of you.

154
00:09:44,463 --> 00:09:45,922
[HOLMES chuckles]
Still lying.

155
00:09:45,964 --> 00:09:48,216
I swear to you, I'm not!

156
00:09:48,258 --> 00:09:49,842
[ADLER chuckles]

157
00:09:50,802 --> 00:09:55,474
[ADLER] Promise me one thing.
You won't forget about me?

158
00:09:55,515 --> 00:09:58,935
I couldn't forget
even if I wanted to.

159
00:09:58,977 --> 00:10:02,481
[ADLER]
Farewell, my detective.

160
00:10:13,617 --> 00:10:18,371
[HOLMES] As long as you're
alive, I know we'll meet again.

161
00:10:21,541 --> 00:10:24,544
[footsteps]

162
00:10:27,422 --> 00:10:30,758
There's a passageway
like this beneath the church?

163
00:10:34,304 --> 00:10:35,805
[gasps]

164
00:10:38,475 --> 00:10:40,435
Holmes made an appearance,
like you said.

165
00:10:40,477 --> 00:10:42,812
And the transaction
concluded smoothly.

166
00:10:42,854 --> 00:10:45,607
Your cunning plan
saved us, Will, again.

167
00:10:45,649 --> 00:10:47,651
[WILLIAM]
Excellent to hear, Brother.

168
00:10:47,692 --> 00:10:48,776
[ADLER]
By the sound of it,

169
00:10:48,818 --> 00:10:51,988
they were anticipating
Sherlock's interference.

170
00:10:52,030 --> 00:10:53,698
Is it possible?

171
00:10:53,739 --> 00:10:55,783
No, there's no doubt about it.

172
00:10:55,825 --> 00:10:57,743
When it comes to
the Lord of Crime,

173
00:10:57,785 --> 00:11:01,289
the title doesn't refer
to a single one person.

174
00:11:01,331 --> 00:11:04,543
As for the heart of
the organization...

175
00:11:07,420 --> 00:11:11,049
My life is in your hands,
I pledge my service.

176
00:11:11,090 --> 00:11:12,925
And in exchange
for your loyalty,

177
00:11:12,967 --> 00:11:16,513
I shall bestow upon you
what you desire most.

178
00:11:16,555 --> 00:11:18,890
Come, Irene Adler.

179
00:11:18,931 --> 00:11:20,600
[grunts]

180
00:11:20,642 --> 00:11:21,809
I believe you and I should

181
00:11:21,851 --> 00:11:24,979
make our way to
the final negotiation.

182
00:11:42,914 --> 00:11:44,957
It seems I was mistaken.

183
00:11:44,999 --> 00:11:47,793
And here I thought you
were smarter than this.

184
00:11:54,551 --> 00:11:56,344
You managed to
recover the document,

185
00:11:56,386 --> 00:11:58,221
as well as liquidate Adler.

186
00:11:58,263 --> 00:12:01,099
At least, that's what was
written in your telegram.

187
00:12:02,684 --> 00:12:05,270
I trust there's an explanation.

188
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:10,900
[ALBERT] The contents
proved extremely fascinating.

189
00:12:10,942 --> 00:12:13,486
Who could have ever
guessed the French Revolution

190
00:12:13,528 --> 00:12:16,406
was a social
experiment set up by us?

191
00:12:16,448 --> 00:12:19,325
In addition, that
Maximilien Robespierre,

192
00:12:19,367 --> 00:12:22,870
the mastermind behind the plot,
and author of the document,

193
00:12:22,912 --> 00:12:26,666
was an agent working
for Britain all along.

194
00:12:26,708 --> 00:12:29,835
Indeed, these pages
detail the exact effort

195
00:12:29,877 --> 00:12:31,463
used by the British Empire

196
00:12:31,504 --> 00:12:35,550
to instigate the upheaval
of French society.

197
00:12:35,592 --> 00:12:38,010
Imagine if these papers
were ever made public.

198
00:12:38,052 --> 00:12:40,597
Our allied nations would
be completely justified

199
00:12:40,639 --> 00:12:42,974
in going to war
against us in retaliation

200
00:12:43,015 --> 00:12:45,935
for meddling in another
country's affairs.

201
00:12:47,562 --> 00:12:50,315
I grow increasingly
weary of these games.

202
00:12:50,356 --> 00:12:51,983
My sole interest is ascertaining

203
00:12:52,024 --> 00:12:54,319
whether you're an
enemy of Britain.

204
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:57,863
[ALBERT] And I have but
a single request of you:

205
00:12:57,905 --> 00:12:59,907
your absolute silence.

206
00:12:59,949 --> 00:13:03,161
[MYCROFT grunts]

207
00:13:03,202 --> 00:13:04,621
[ALBERT]
Ever since I was young,

208
00:13:04,663 --> 00:13:06,748
I have sought to
expose corruption.

209
00:13:06,790 --> 00:13:09,334
To bring to light the
misdeeds of the nobility

210
00:13:09,375 --> 00:13:11,670
in an effort to collapse
the class system.

211
00:13:11,711 --> 00:13:13,129
[MYCROFT]
I see.

212
00:13:13,171 --> 00:13:15,590
So, you're the one
everybody's talking about,

213
00:13:15,632 --> 00:13:17,801
the "Lord of Crime."

214
00:13:17,842 --> 00:13:20,720
[WILLIAM] Guilty. Everything
that has transpired

215
00:13:20,762 --> 00:13:23,556
has been engineered
to further our goal.

216
00:13:23,598 --> 00:13:27,893
Collectively, we are
"James Moriarty."

217
00:13:27,935 --> 00:13:29,813
Unmasking yourself now?

218
00:13:29,854 --> 00:13:32,857
My investigation revealed you
had effective collaborators.

219
00:13:32,898 --> 00:13:34,859
If I'm not mistaken, you are...

220
00:13:34,900 --> 00:13:37,945
Call me William,
Director Holmes.

221
00:13:37,987 --> 00:13:42,325
The Lord of Crime accompanied
by both his left and right hand.

222
00:13:42,367 --> 00:13:44,118
As for our ultimate objective--

223
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:46,371
it's the same as the
author of these papers:

224
00:13:46,412 --> 00:13:50,458
rid the world of tyrants and
bring equality to our homeland.

225
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:52,084
The leader of
the French Revolution

226
00:13:52,126 --> 00:13:54,420
was Maximilien Robespierre.

227
00:13:54,462 --> 00:13:57,215
Following the execution of
King Louis the 16th,

228
00:13:57,256 --> 00:14:00,426
he abruptly preached for the
necessity of the Reign of Terror

229
00:14:00,468 --> 00:14:02,804
and carried out the purge.

230
00:14:04,681 --> 00:14:05,849
[WILLIAM]
History has painted him

231
00:14:05,890 --> 00:14:08,100
as one of the great villains
behind the Revolution.

232
00:14:08,142 --> 00:14:10,228
His actions were
difficult to comprehend

233
00:14:10,269 --> 00:14:11,730
through conventional thinking.

234
00:14:11,771 --> 00:14:15,567
However, there was
a reason behind the madness.

235
00:14:15,608 --> 00:14:18,069
His goal was to
overthrow the monarchy

236
00:14:18,110 --> 00:14:21,740
and place control of the country
in the hands of its people.

237
00:14:23,199 --> 00:14:25,243
[WILLIAM]
He managed to execute the king

238
00:14:25,284 --> 00:14:28,079
and the revolution
appeared to be a success.

239
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:29,873
However...

240
00:14:29,914 --> 00:14:33,167
...as a direct result of
vilifying the ruling class,

241
00:14:33,209 --> 00:14:36,254
the people clamoured for
the nobility to be killed.

242
00:14:36,295 --> 00:14:40,091
The situation quickly
spiralled out of his control.

243
00:14:40,132 --> 00:14:45,304
In response, he decided
to adopt a new measure...

244
00:14:45,346 --> 00:14:48,600
...what became known
as the Reign of Terror.

245
00:14:49,809 --> 00:14:51,269
[WILLIAM]
Aristocrats and citizens

246
00:14:51,310 --> 00:14:53,813
who opposed the
revolution were executed,

247
00:14:53,855 --> 00:14:56,357
one after another.

248
00:14:57,567 --> 00:14:59,527
[WILLIAM]
The indiscriminate bloodshed

249
00:14:59,569 --> 00:15:00,445
turned the people's ire

250
00:15:00,486 --> 00:15:03,656
from the nobility
onto Robespierre.

251
00:15:04,990 --> 00:15:08,077
[WILLIAM] He created a common
enemy for both sides to loath.

252
00:15:08,119 --> 00:15:12,039
[CROWD shouting]

253
00:15:12,081 --> 00:15:13,374
[WOMAN 14A]
Death to all tyrants!

254
00:15:13,416 --> 00:15:16,669
[WILLIAM] The Terror was put
to rest with one last death:

255
00:15:16,711 --> 00:15:18,463
his own.

256
00:15:19,756 --> 00:15:21,674
And now, we're
attempting to achieve

257
00:15:21,716 --> 00:15:24,886
the same results for
Britain in these modern times.

258
00:15:26,596 --> 00:15:29,056
[WILLIAM] Our aim is to
redistribute power,

259
00:15:29,098 --> 00:15:31,517
dividing it as
equally as possible.

260
00:15:31,559 --> 00:15:33,311
By employing crime to that end,

261
00:15:33,352 --> 00:15:35,563
we will become
the common "evil."

262
00:15:35,605 --> 00:15:38,483
Despised by both the
nobility and the people,

263
00:15:38,524 --> 00:15:41,820
allowing both sides
to unite hand-in-hand.

264
00:15:41,861 --> 00:15:43,655
Eventually, we will
meet the same fate

265
00:15:43,696 --> 00:15:45,490
that befell Robespierre.

266
00:15:45,531 --> 00:15:47,992
When the full weight of
our sins comes to light,

267
00:15:48,033 --> 00:15:51,078
the Moriartys will have to die.

268
00:15:52,330 --> 00:15:55,291
[ALBERT] Now that you know
our plans, what will yours be?

269
00:15:56,334 --> 00:15:58,043
If you wish to
sacrifice yourselves

270
00:15:58,085 --> 00:15:59,921
in an act of patriotism,
go ahead.

271
00:15:59,963 --> 00:16:02,006
I've no intention
of interfering.

272
00:16:02,047 --> 00:16:03,341
That is, however,

273
00:16:03,382 --> 00:16:07,094
assuming the three of you
really are patriots.

274
00:16:07,136 --> 00:16:10,139
If I decide at any time
you are out of control,

275
00:16:10,181 --> 00:16:12,099
then as enemies of Britain,

276
00:16:12,141 --> 00:16:15,770
you will be eliminated.
That is a promise.

277
00:16:15,812 --> 00:16:17,313
As would be your right.

278
00:16:17,355 --> 00:16:20,024
There is a reason why we
revealed ourselves to you.

279
00:16:20,065 --> 00:16:23,361
There are those who say you are
the government itself.

280
00:16:24,654 --> 00:16:25,905
Very well, then.

281
00:16:25,947 --> 00:16:27,866
Speaking on behalf of
the British government,

282
00:16:27,907 --> 00:16:29,200
you have my solemn word.

283
00:16:29,241 --> 00:16:31,828
We'll remain silent
towards your activity.

284
00:16:31,870 --> 00:16:34,413
You have our
gratitude, Director.

285
00:16:36,290 --> 00:16:40,044
This is yours, sir, but
permit me to ask one question.

286
00:16:40,085 --> 00:16:42,672
Why keep this document
instead of destroying it?

287
00:16:42,714 --> 00:16:46,217
You continue to run the risk
of it being stolen again.

288
00:16:46,258 --> 00:16:48,803
Surely there has to be a reason.

289
00:16:50,054 --> 00:16:52,724
Two reasons actually.

290
00:16:52,765 --> 00:16:56,060
First, her Majesty feels that
the failure of this mission

291
00:16:56,101 --> 00:16:57,186
is a crime for which Britain

292
00:16:57,228 --> 00:16:59,564
must shoulder
the weight indefinitely.

293
00:16:59,605 --> 00:17:01,399
The other reason
is more personal.

294
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:03,192
See, Maximilien Robespierre,

295
00:17:03,234 --> 00:17:06,612
the author responsible for
penning this document--

296
00:17:06,654 --> 00:17:09,866
his true name was
Sherrinford Holmes.

297
00:17:09,908 --> 00:17:11,034
[gasps]

298
00:17:11,075 --> 00:17:13,536
[MYCROFT]
An ancestor of mine.

299
00:17:13,578 --> 00:17:18,082
This is our family's punishment,
one we must continue to bear.

300
00:17:18,123 --> 00:17:19,584
And the reason why I continue

301
00:17:19,625 --> 00:17:22,587
to pledge loyalty to
the British Government.

302
00:17:24,088 --> 00:17:25,130
[MYCROFT chuckles]

303
00:17:25,172 --> 00:17:27,132
My dear brother's not
aware of any of this.

304
00:17:27,174 --> 00:17:28,509
You can understand.

305
00:17:28,551 --> 00:17:31,679
I prefer him to live
free of the knowledge.

306
00:17:31,721 --> 00:17:34,265
Now then, enough
of this idle talk.

307
00:17:35,767 --> 00:17:37,894
[gasps]

308
00:17:40,605 --> 00:17:44,108
[MYCROFT]
Our deal has been struck.

309
00:17:48,571 --> 00:17:52,658
[PEOPLE chattering]

310
00:17:57,789 --> 00:18:01,375
[MYCROFT] I trust I find you
in good health, Doctor Watson.

311
00:18:01,417 --> 00:18:03,628
[WATSON]
Mycroft, hello.

312
00:18:03,669 --> 00:18:05,504
Did you need to
speak with Sherlock?

313
00:18:05,546 --> 00:18:08,424
I'm afraid it appears he's
stepped out for the moment.

314
00:18:08,466 --> 00:18:11,343
Yes, perhaps it is
better this way.

315
00:18:11,385 --> 00:18:12,929
[WATSON]
Hm?

316
00:18:12,971 --> 00:18:16,557
There is a woman for whom
my brother has given his all.

317
00:18:16,599 --> 00:18:19,894
He may even have had
special feelings for her.

318
00:18:19,936 --> 00:18:21,813
That is why I wanted to come

319
00:18:21,854 --> 00:18:24,649
and tell him
about this directly.

320
00:18:47,005 --> 00:18:51,509
Good night and goodbye,
Mister Sherlock Holmes.

321
00:18:52,468 --> 00:18:54,679
[HOLMES grunts]

322
00:19:04,856 --> 00:19:05,690
[HUDSON, WATSON grunt]

323
00:19:05,731 --> 00:19:06,774
Sherlock, I...

324
00:19:06,816 --> 00:19:07,566
[HUDSON sobs]

325
00:19:07,608 --> 00:19:09,110
What's the matter with you two?

326
00:19:09,152 --> 00:19:11,195
You look as if you've
seen a ghost or something.

327
00:19:11,236 --> 00:19:13,572
[BOTH grunt]

328
00:19:13,614 --> 00:19:16,408
[WATSON]
Actually, you see...

329
00:19:16,450 --> 00:19:19,537
...Mycroft came by
with a message for you.

330
00:19:19,578 --> 00:19:23,290
Word is... Miss Adler
has passed away.

331
00:19:23,332 --> 00:19:26,585
And that her body was
pulled out of the Thames.

332
00:19:38,305 --> 00:19:39,515
[ALBERT]
If there comes a time when you

333
00:19:39,557 --> 00:19:41,976
determine she has
been dispatched,

334
00:19:42,018 --> 00:19:43,853
you're free to
open the envelope,

335
00:19:43,895 --> 00:19:47,106
read my name,
and then come for me.

336
00:19:58,534 --> 00:20:00,369
[chuckles]

337
00:20:16,468 --> 00:20:21,015
[HOLMES]
She's dead. "The woman" is dead.

338
00:20:26,187 --> 00:20:30,524
[HOLMES]
That's the truth, isn't it?

339
00:20:34,070 --> 00:20:37,907
[ALBERT] It's time to
carry out our final job.

340
00:20:40,284 --> 00:20:42,620
[ALBERT] Go, Fred, and
select a body from the morgue

341
00:20:42,661 --> 00:20:45,248
that'll prove to be a
suitable stand-in for her.

342
00:20:45,289 --> 00:20:47,041
[FRED]
It shall be done.

343
00:20:47,083 --> 00:20:49,293
Irene, as of this moment,

344
00:20:49,334 --> 00:20:52,004
you are no longer
among the living.

345
00:20:52,046 --> 00:20:54,465
You are a member
of this organization

346
00:20:54,506 --> 00:20:56,842
and we're going
to put you to work.

347
00:20:56,884 --> 00:20:58,427
Right.

348
00:20:59,637 --> 00:21:02,765
It goes without saying
you'll need a new identity.

349
00:21:02,807 --> 00:21:04,725
For your first name,
we'll give you ours.

350
00:21:04,767 --> 00:21:07,645
Thus, you'll be known as James.

351
00:21:07,686 --> 00:21:09,563
As for your last name...

352
00:21:09,605 --> 00:21:12,357
This marks the
start of a new life.

353
00:21:12,399 --> 00:21:16,487
New friends. New bonds...

354
00:21:48,769 --> 00:21:51,105
My name should reflect that.

355
00:21:51,147 --> 00:21:53,732
The name is James Bonde.

356
00:23:32,748 --> 00:23:35,626
[BONDE] Next time on
Moriarty the Patriot  :

357
00:23:35,667 --> 00:23:38,837
"The Phantom of
Whitechapel Act One."
